podman unshare only works in rootless mode - i.e., when you're running Podman as a regular user. If you're running as actual root (UID 0), Podman will refuse to run unshare because:

1. Root doesn't need user namespaces - root already has full privileges
2. It's a conflict - you're asking for "fake root" when you're already real root

